          "anchor": "conclusion",
          "quote": "We set out to make a 2B reasoner think less, and found that the base model's real problem was not thinking too much but never stopping. A correctness-gated length penalty, placed only in the reward and optimized with stock GRPO, largely fixes that in distribution, within 200 LoRA updates on one consumer GPU: it cuts thinking by three quarters and doubles strict accuracy. None of the refinements we tried improved on it.",
